WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
Boxing Day, 2015.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:07.190
The River Aire in Leeds reaches some
of the highest levels ever recorded.

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.950
Nearly 3,000 homes and 700
business properties are affected.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.180
In 2017, Leeds opens moveable weirs: the
first used for flood alleviation in the

5
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:18.950
UK.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.050
When a flood is coming, their gates
are lowered on inflatable bladders.

7
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.110
It takes about two hours.

8
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.790
Why lay a barrier flat
just as a flood arrives?

9
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.170
So boats can pass?

10
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.110
In this mission, you'll
find out what Leeds built,

11
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.570
from the centre to the upper river.

12
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.750
Then you'll weigh its issues
for people, money and the river.

13
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: find out why the Leeds
weir gates go down when a flood comes.
